(269191, 18126, 6523, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition of this photo -- it''s got a very nice sense of movement.  I''m not a big fan of frames on the digital photos, but in this case, I think it really helps containing the large amount of blue sky.  Good work!</td>', 'I really like the composition of this photo -- it''s got a very nice sense of movement.  I''m not a big fan of frames on the digital photos, but in this case, I think it really helps containing the large amount of blue sky.  Good work!', '2003-04-17 01:40:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(269192, 18259, 6523, '<td valign="top">Is that really snow?  I never saw anything like that before.  It''s pretty neat!  How on earth did you get up there to take the photo?  On a ladder?  (I love photos that make me wonder how they were made.)</td>', 'Is that really snow?  I never saw anything like that before.  It''s pretty neat!  How on earth did you get up there to take the photo?  On a ladder?  (I love photos that make me wonder how they were made.)', '2003-04-17 01:42:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(269195, 18233, 6523, '<td valign="top">I think the blur of the fountain detracts from the overall image -- I would have cropped the fountain out completely -- I guess that means I would have cropped down to ONLY the silhouette and the sky.  Still, it''s a very beautiful sunset!</td>', 'I think the blur of the fountain detracts from the overall image -- I would have cropped the fountain out completely -- I guess that means I would have cropped down to ONLY the silhouette and the sky.  Still, it''s a very beautiful sunset!', '2003-04-17 01:47:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(269196, 18257, 6523, '<td valign="top">I love your sky, but I think if you''d had a little something from the land in the photo, the picture would have seemed a bit more solid.  Definitely a cool sky, though.</td>', 'I love your sky, but I think if you''d had a little something from the land in the photo, the picture would have seemed a bit more solid.  Definitely a cool sky, though.', '2003-04-17 01:49:34.000000', NULL, 1),
