(272172, 17625, 1041, '<td valign="top"><b>A Comment From The Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Danny :)<br/> <br/>Well, if I''m supposed to suggest areas for improvement then this is going to be a very very short critique.  :)<br/> <br/>First of, congratulations on your ribbon, it''s very well deserved, this is a spectacular image.  The title very aptly describes the image, I love how the sun is shining through the tree and almost gives it a halo that is then surrounded by black clouds and then above that you have yet another burst of color and rays, shooting straight up into the air.<br/> <br/>I think that, other than the obvious dramatic quality of the photo, it is the somewhat atypical approach to a sunset that makes this shot.  The vertical format is more unusual and the really dark clouds and lack of obvious horizon aren''t part of the more standard sunset image, either.  <br/> <br/>The frame very nicely enhances the image.  I''m always at awe when people manage to take photos that don''t need a lot of tweaking, you certainly did that, too.<br/> <br/>Again, congratulations on a very well deserved ribbon :)<br/> <br/>Please let me know if you have any questions or comments about this review.<br/> <br/>Franziska.</td>', 'A Comment From The Critique Club  Hi Danny :) Well, if I''m supposed to suggest areas for improvement then this is going to be a very very short critique.  :) First of, congratulations on your ribbon, it''s very well deserved, this is a spectacular image.  The title very aptly describes the image, I love how the sun is shining through the tree and almost gives it a halo that is then surrounded by black clouds and then above that you have yet another burst of color and rays, shooting straight up into the air. I think that, other than the obvious dramatic quality of the photo, it is the somewhat atypical approach to a sunset that makes this shot.  The vertical format is more unusual and the really dark clouds and lack of obvious horizon aren''t part of the more standard sunset image, either.   The frame very nicely enhances the image.  I''m always at awe when people manage to take photos that don''t need a lot of tweaking, you certainly did that, too. Again, congratulations on a very well deserved ribbon :) Please let me know if you have any questions or comments about this review. Franziska.', '2003-04-21 11:32:08.000000', NULL, 0),
