INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(273249, 18259, 5865, '<td valign="top">That''s a really interesting shot Karma.  You did well to capture it.<br/> <br/>Anthony.</td>', 'That''s a really interesting shot Karma.  You did well to capture it. Anthony.', '2003-04-22 07:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(273342, 18147, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Myqyl...<br/> <br/>As I mentioned earlier in the challenge, I really enjoyed this photo.  I like shots like this one where the vast expanse of sky with the wispy clouds is highlighted by a thin strip of interesting landscape on the bottom of the frame.  The clouds in this scene really make a strong impression... The gradient of dark to light blue in your sky is also excellent. This photo kinda makes me think of the ''old man and the sea'' theme... maybe this is a little fishing village on some stretch of rural coastline... It''s fun to try to visualize some sort of story to go along with certain photos :)<br/> <br/>I don''t really have any suggestions for improvement on this photo.  I quite like it the way it is :)<br/> <br/>Keep up the great work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Myqyl... As I mentioned earlier in the challenge, I really enjoyed this photo.  I like shots like this one where the vast expanse of sky with the wispy clouds is highlighted by a thin strip of interesting landscape on the bottom of the frame.  The clouds in this scene really make a strong impression... The gradient of dark to light blue in your sky is also excellent. This photo kinda makes me think of the ''old man and the sea'' theme... maybe this is a little fishing village on some stretch of rural coastline... It''s fun to try to visualize some sort of story to go along with certain photos :) I don''t really have any suggestions for improvement on this photo.  I quite like it the way it is :) Keep up the great work :) John Setzler', '2003-04-22 10:10:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(273346, 18087, 7466, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I agree wholeheartedly with you, this tree has great character and apparently a camera hound spirit if it called you back several times ;).<br/> <br/>The composition is great on the shot.  I like the off-center placement of the tree in question and the host of others scattered about it.<br/> <br/>The focus and clarity is wonderful.  Nice and crisp with great contrast between the darkness of the aged wood and the green of new pine needles.<br/> <br/>Overall, a great shot and something I would have gone after if I''d see that great tree myself LOL.<br/> <br/>Shari</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) I agree wholeheartedly with you, this tree has great character and apparently a camera hound spirit if it called you back several times ;). The composition is great on the shot.  I like the off-center placement of the tree in question and the host of others scattered about it. The focus and clarity is wonderful.  Nice and crisp with great contrast between the darkness of the aged wood and the green of new pine needles. Overall, a great shot and something I would have gone after if I''d see that great tree myself LOL. Shari', '2003-04-22 10:15:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(273348, 18071, 7466, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I really like the sillouettes in this shot.  The large cactus just off center is a great balance to the sun.  I like the striated clouds below the darkness as well.<br/> <br/>My only contention with this shot is the amount of dark sky above the features.  I think a tighter crop would have given the shot a heavier impact.  As it is, I feel as though the large dark swath drags the composition down.<br/> <br/>Otherwise, I think it''s a fabulous shot that you captured very well.<br/> <br/>Shari</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) I really like the sillouettes in this shot.  The large cactus just off center is a great balance to the sun.  I like the striated clouds below the darkness as well. My only contention with this shot is the amount of dark sky above the features.  I think a tighter crop would have given the shot a heavier impact.  As it is, I feel as though the large dark swath drags the composition down. Otherwise, I think it''s a fabulous shot that you captured very well. Shari', '2003-04-22 10:19:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(273354, 17908, 5728, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Hi Shari. I didn''t enter a weather submission because all we had during the challenge week was blue skies. Not even a few clouds at all, if there had been at least a few clouds I might have done something like you did.<br/> <br/>Like I mentioned in my comment below I like the effect of the blue sky starting darker on the left and progressing lighter the more you look to the right. And in contrast the clouds below the sky have the opposite effect going from dark on the right to light on the left.<br/> <br/>The blue sky is a little grainy but it is difficult to shoot the sky without getting a certain amount of grain in the image.<br/> <br/>All in all a simple pic of the sky which you can''t really do to much wrong with. Well done.<br/> <br/>Gary</td>', 'Critique Club: Hi Shari. I didn''t enter a weather submission because all we had during the challenge week was blue skies. Not even a few clouds at all, if there had been at least a few clouds I might have done something like you did. Like I mentioned in my comment below I like the effect of the blue sky starting darker on the left and progressing lighter the more you look to the right. And in contrast the clouds below the sky have the opposite effect going from dark on the right to light on the left. The blue sky is a little grainy but it is difficult to shoot the sky without getting a certain amount of grain in the image. All in all a simple pic of the sky which you can''t really do to much wrong with. Well done. Gary', '2003-04-22 10:35:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(273358, 18276, 5728, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Hi E.J. Again I have the honor of critiquing your photo. This is one of those shots I would have thought would do a lot better. I really like this pic a lot, but you can never foretell how the rest of the DPC voters will vote right?<br/> <br/>The lighting is perfect here, the detail is amazing, those water drops look just so crisp. The decision to do this in black and white was okay, I think it has come out well, although a lot of comments below state they would rather have seen this in color.<br/> <br/>The cropping is something I would have done differently, the main subject seems just a little too centered for me.<br/> <br/>Apart from that I think you did a good job.<br/> <br/>Gary</td>', 'Critique Club: Hi E.J. Again I have the honor of critiquing your photo. This is one of those shots I would have thought would do a lot better. I really like this pic a lot, but you can never foretell how the rest of the DPC voters will vote right? The lighting is perfect here, the detail is amazing, those water drops look just so crisp. The decision to do this in black and white was okay, I think it has come out well, although a lot of comments below state they would rather have seen this in color. The cropping is something I would have done differently, the main subject seems just a little too centered for me. Apart from that I think you did a good job. Gary', '2003-04-22 10:48:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(273400, 17921, 7843, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Mr Bell. I new your shot would be in the running but the Yellow Ribbon... you must be double chuffed as it''s your first submission. Nice one man!</td>', 'Congratulations Mr Bell. I new your shot would be in the running but the Yellow Ribbon... you must be double chuffed as it''s your first submission. Nice one man!', '2003-04-22 11:40:13.000000', NULL, 0),
