(273909, 18244, 1031, '<td valign="top">I really liked this, but was a little "suspicious" since I''d already been to this site for <a href="//arch.ced.berkeley.edu/kap/index.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Kite Aerial Photography</a>. Good job creating a convincing representation!</td>', 'I really liked this, but was a little "suspicious" since I''d already been to this site for Kite Aerial Photography. Good job creating a convincing representation!', '2003-04-22 22:28:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(273921, 17705, 6870, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I concur with all of the compliments below!<br/> <br/>In this photo, I see a very close up of a rose, with all of its lovely colors and textures. The petals create interesting shadows for me and the water drops add even more complexity to this perceiveably simple subject. Your superb lighting brings out colors, textures and shadows quite well. I see in your photo a comunication, however deliberate or subliminal on your part, that beauty is all around us, even up close. I also infer a sense that nature can be lovely despite the weather. This is made even more effective by your close and from-the-side perspective. So your image works for me.<br/> <br/>For improvement, you have a lot of comments to sharpen your focus, and it is true that doing this would enhance the loveliness and impact of the photo. Other than that, this is a really nice shot. It is amazing that focus would lower your score that much, but we''re a persnickity group when it comes to that, I guess.<br/> <br/>Good luck! I hope to see more of your work in the future!<br/> <br/>David</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I concur with all of the compliments below! In this photo, I see a very close up of a rose, with all of its lovely colors and textures. The petals create interesting shadows for me and the water drops add even more complexity to this perceiveably simple subject. Your superb lighting brings out colors, textures and shadows quite well. I see in your photo a comunication, however deliberate or subliminal on your part, that beauty is all around us, even up close. I also infer a sense that nature can be lovely despite the weather. This is made even more effective by your close and from-the-side perspective. So your image works for me. For improvement, you have a lot of comments to sharpen your focus, and it is true that doing this would enhance the loveliness and impact of the photo. Other than that, this is a really nice shot. It is amazing that focus would lower your score that much, but we''re a persnickity group when it comes to that, I guess. Good luck! I hope to see more of your work in the future! David', '2003-04-22 22:39:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(273933, 18161, 4340, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JasonPR:</b></div><hr/><i>whether or not it''s about weather, it''s still a great shot.  I wish I could have gotten such a good shot for the fauna challenge.  I''ve added this to my favorites.  Great job.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!  I realize it would''ve been more appropriate for the fauna challenge. (Well, how was I to know that would''ve been the topic for this week?)Anyway as an explanation, I don''t think I would''ve been able to get this relaxed shot were it not for the heat in Texas.  It was running away from me all the time, but was hot one afternoon and didn''t feel like moving because it was obviously tired from the heat.  The challenge guidelines said something about the effects of climate on the environment, and this is the environment!  Jitams</td>', 'Originally posted by JasonPR:whether or not it''s about weather, it''s still a great shot.  I wish I could have gotten such a good shot for the fauna challenge.  I''ve added this to my favorites.  Great job.  Thanks!  I realize it would''ve been more appropriate for the fauna challenge. (Well, how was I to know that would''ve been the topic for this week?)Anyway as an explanation, I don''t think I would''ve been able to get this relaxed shot were it not for the heat in Texas.  It was running away from me all the time, but was hot one afternoon and didn''t feel like moving because it was obviously tired from the heat.  The challenge guidelines said something about the effects of climate on the environment, and this is the environment!  Jitams', '2003-04-22 23:09:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(273993, 17625, 7706, '<td valign="top">I don''t think I can really say anything that has not been said already. Just wow!</td>', 'I don''t think I can really say anything that has not been said already. Just wow!', '2003-04-23 00:43:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(274214, 18244, 6870, '<td valign="top">You Fiend! That was my idea! Oh well, I think you did it better than I would have done. Nice work!</td>', 'You Fiend! That was my idea! Oh well, I think you did it better than I would have done. Nice work!', '2003-04-23 01:54:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(274467, 17891, 1717, '<td valign="top">GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB :)<br/> <br/>This is a great photo!  The exposure is very nice and the rocks in the foreground give some really nice perspective.<br/> <br/>The only reason I can see for the score not being higher is that it''s a little difficult to tie it in to the weather challenge.  Although there is always weather around us, I think most voters were looking for something dramatic...clouds, storms, sunsets.  As a result of that, this photo suffered.<br/> <br/>Standing alone, without the confines of the challenge, this is a beautiful photo.  Be proud.<br/> <br/>Take care...<br/>Sher<br/> <br/></td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB :) This is a great photo!  The exposure is very nice and the rocks in the foreground give some really nice perspective. The only reason I can see for the score not being higher is that it''s a little difficult to tie it in to the weather challenge.  Although there is always weather around us, I think most voters were looking for something dramatic...clouds, storms, sunsets.  As a result of that, this photo suffered. Standing alone, without the confines of the challenge, this is a beautiful photo.  Be proud. Take care...Sher ', '2003-04-23 03:31:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(274716, 17905, 7466, '<td valign="top">Greatings from the critique club :)<br/> <br/>I really like the concept of this photo.  My first thought was of the silent French film from the 1970s called "The Red Balloon."  I think the dim lighting and greyish overtone are fabulous and definitely gives the feel of a rainy afternoon.  However, I think the composition of the shot is lacking in a couple of areas.  <br/> <br/>First, the fence is very hard on the eyes.  I almost get dizzy looking at it and it distracts the eye from what should be the obvious focal point:  the red umbrella.<br/> <br/>Second, the white line on the asphalt (basketball key, I''m guessing), also pulls the eye from the umbrella.  It''s a bold stripe of contrast before the eye reaches the umbrella.<br/> <br/>Perhaps a slightly different angle to better use the lines as leading lines and a tighter crop to eliminate as much of the fence as possible would have made this a stronger photograph.<br/> <br/> <br/>Shari<br/></td>', 'Greatings from the critique club :) I really like the concept of this photo.  My first thought was of the silent French film from the 1970s called "The Red Balloon."  I think the dim lighting and greyish overtone are fabulous and definitely gives the feel of a rainy afternoon.  However, I think the composition of the shot is lacking in a couple of areas.   First, the fence is very hard on the eyes.  I almost get dizzy looking at it and it distracts the eye from what should be the obvious focal point:  the red umbrella. Second, the white line on the asphalt (basketball key, I''m guessing), also pulls the eye from the umbrella.  It''s a bold stripe of contrast before the eye reaches the umbrella. Perhaps a slightly different angle to better use the lines as leading lines and a tighter crop to eliminate as much of the fence as possible would have made this a stronger photograph.  Shari', '2003-04-23 10:13:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(274728, 17658, 7466, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I like this shot an awful lot.  The clarity of focus is great.  The DOF makes the railing a clear focal point.  The colors are crisp and beautiful.<br/> <br/>I think the only problem I see with this shot is that the out of focus rain drops in the background are a little distracting.  I know what they are and why they are there, but on the surface they look like streaks on the photo.  I don''t know how you might avoid them and if I had taken this shot, I probably would have striven to have them.<br/> <br/>Keep up the great work, this is a wonderful photo.<br/> <br/>Shari</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) I like this shot an awful lot.  The clarity of focus is great.  The DOF makes the railing a clear focal point.  The colors are crisp and beautiful. I think the only problem I see with this shot is that the out of focus rain drops in the background are a little distracting.  I know what they are and why they are there, but on the surface they look like streaks on the photo.  I don''t know how you might avoid them and if I had taken this shot, I probably would have striven to have them. Keep up the great work, this is a wonderful photo. Shari', '2003-04-23 10:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(274762, 18158, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - Generally this is a nice pic.  I think the subject is a little lacking, but it is a very well taken photo.  There really isn''t too much specifically wrong with the composition.  The thing I like most about it is the branch coming from the top left of the picture down to meet the other branches.  It makes for good perspective.  It gives us kind of a leading line.  The aspect ratio of this photo is a little troubling for me.  I would''ve rather seen it in a different portrait ratio where it isn''t this thin.<br/> <br/>Technical - I really like the way this was taken.  I think the DOF you used is optimal for this.  The branch leading down from the top is mostly in focus.  The stuff underneath isn''t, but we know what it is.  The tonal quality of the pic is nice.  The brownness of it makes it like sort of a sepia.  It makes for a nice pic.<br/> <br/>Overall - Not a bad photo at all, just not a real compelling subject.  Very well taken and the color choice is good.  If it matters, I kinda like the border.  THe other commenters didn''t generally like it but I think it works.  I have to agree with some of them on the aspect ratio thing.  Well that''s about all I have to add.  Good luck in future challenges - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - Generally this is a nice pic.  I think the subject is a little lacking, but it is a very well taken photo.  There really isn''t too much specifically wrong with the composition.  The thing I like most about it is the branch coming from the top left of the picture down to meet the other branches.  It makes for good perspective.  It gives us kind of a leading line.  The aspect ratio of this photo is a little troubling for me.  I would''ve rather seen it in a different portrait ratio where it isn''t this thin. Technical - I really like the way this was taken.  I think the DOF you used is optimal for this.  The branch leading down from the top is mostly in focus.  The stuff underneath isn''t, but we know what it is.  The tonal quality of the pic is nice.  The brownness of it makes it like sort of a sepia.  It makes for a nice pic. Overall - Not a bad photo at all, just not a real compelling subject.  Very well taken and the color choice is good.  If it matters, I kinda like the border.  THe other commenters didn''t generally like it but I think it works.  I have to agree with some of them on the aspect ratio thing.  Well that''s about all I have to add.  Good luck in future challenges - Inspzil', '2003-04-23 10:46:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(274979, 17849, 6458, '<td valign="top">Greets from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial Impression:<br/>A plethora of blue, neat idea. Missing something.<br/> <br/>Challenge:<br/>This meets the challenge perfectly in my opinion.<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/>There''s not much to say here, I think you''ve done well for your subject matter. Maybe cropping out the top third would have made it a bit more digestable to the eye, but I think that''s personal preference.<br/> <br/>Technical:<br/>The blue is definitely there and it serves to invoke a melencholy mood. I would like to see a little more contrast to darken the tree branches up, but not too much. <br/> <br/>Overall:<br/>Good weather shot, definitely suits the challenge and stirs emotion in me. Good job. <br/></td>', 'Greets from the Critique Club! Initial Impression:A plethora of blue, neat idea. Missing something. Challenge:This meets the challenge perfectly in my opinion. Composition:There''s not much to say here, I think you''ve done well for your subject matter. Maybe cropping out the top third would have made it a bit more digestable to the eye, but I think that''s personal preference. Technical:The blue is definitely there and it serves to invoke a melencholy mood. I would like to see a little more contrast to darken the tree branches up, but not too much.  Overall:Good weather shot, definitely suits the challenge and stirs emotion in me. Good job. ', '2003-04-23 11:40:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(275148, 18037, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - Excellent composition.  The silhouette is really good and the colors of the sky are beautiful.  Good framing with only a little of the skyline showing at the bottom and the rest just sky.  The vast array of colors across the sky is great, with the reds and oranges at the bottom and the pinks and greys across the top.  Very well done<br/> <br/>Technical - The hard part of this pic is the taking of the picture at the correct exposure.  You did really well on this one, judging by the way I like to see my own photos come out that are similar to this.  The sun is pretty hot in this photo exposure-wise, and it should be because IT''S THE SUN!!!  Now for the sky, I have to say its a little oversaturated looking at the pixelation.  Its just a fuzz too much in my estimation and that''s why it pixelated.  I''m sure thats a lot of the reason the other colors look so good.  I reckon you gotta take the bad with the good.  I don''t think I''d have done the same thing.<br/> <br/>Overall - Beautiful photo and well done for the most part.  I never get sick of a good sunrise or sunset.  Hope this could be a little helpful for you.  Good luck in future challenges. - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - Excellent composition.  The silhouette is really good and the colors of the sky are beautiful.  Good framing with only a little of the skyline showing at the bottom and the rest just sky.  The vast array of colors across the sky is great, with the reds and oranges at the bottom and the pinks and greys across the top.  Very well done Technical - The hard part of this pic is the taking of the picture at the correct exposure.  You did really well on this one, judging by the way I like to see my own photos come out that are similar to this.  The sun is pretty hot in this photo exposure-wise, and it should be because IT''S THE SUN!!!  Now for the sky, I have to say its a little oversaturated looking at the pixelation.  Its just a fuzz too much in my estimation and that''s why it pixelated.  I''m sure thats a lot of the reason the other colors look so good.  I reckon you gotta take the bad with the good.  I don''t think I''d have done the same thing. Overall - Beautiful photo and well done for the most part.  I never get sick of a good sunrise or sunset.  Hope this could be a little helpful for you.  Good luck in future challenges. - Inspzil', '2003-04-23 12:42:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(275182, 18108, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - Really good subject depicted here.  It reminds me of something I''d see in a gardening magazine.  The raindrops look suspiciously like mercury from their very shiny appearance.  I would have cropped the top of this off and some of the right side to in order to really emphasize the 2 leaves that have the cool drops on them.  I think it would''ve brought it into a better perspective with the big main leaf in front, and the smaller leaf as a backup nicely to the left and slightly behind.  You have the DOF to do it and this photo is taken well enough that it would''ve done a lot to enhance the drops on this leaf.<br/> <br/>Technical - This is as well taken as any picture in the whole challenge.  You''ve done a great job with the exposure.  But really on the whole I think this picture is taken as well as you could take it and probably a lot better than I could.  I wouldn''t change anything about the way you took this.<br/> <br/>Overall - A little different crop and I think you''d have had a serious contender on your hands.  It would''ve brought the leaves into pseudo-macro mode and really made them shine even more than they do.  I think a lot of this photo is perception and if you give the viewers only one real thing to see, then they have no choice but to like it :)  At least that''s what I think.  Congrats on a great pic.  Good luck in future challenges - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - Really good subject depicted here.  It reminds me of something I''d see in a gardening magazine.  The raindrops look suspiciously like mercury from their very shiny appearance.  I would have cropped the top of this off and some of the right side to in order to really emphasize the 2 leaves that have the cool drops on them.  I think it would''ve brought it into a better perspective with the big main leaf in front, and the smaller leaf as a backup nicely to the left and slightly behind.  You have the DOF to do it and this photo is taken well enough that it would''ve done a lot to enhance the drops on this leaf. Technical - This is as well taken as any picture in the whole challenge.  You''ve done a great job with the exposure.  But really on the whole I think this picture is taken as well as you could take it and probably a lot better than I could.  I wouldn''t change anything about the way you took this. Overall - A little different crop and I think you''d have had a serious contender on your hands.  It would''ve brought the leaves into pseudo-macro mode and really made them shine even more than they do.  I think a lot of this photo is perception and if you give the viewers only one real thing to see, then they have no choice but to like it :)  At least that''s what I think.  Congrats on a great pic.  Good luck in future challenges - Inspzil', '2003-04-23 12:53:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(275416, 18120, 7711, '<td valign="top">this one was one of my favourites of the challenge. I''m disappointed to see it rank here, I think it was much better than that, I honestly cannot find a thing in it I would change. Great picture, Steve! :)</td>', 'this one was one of my favourites of the challenge. I''m disappointed to see it rank here, I think it was much better than that, I honestly cannot find a thing in it I would change. Great picture, Steve! :)', '2003-04-23 14:09:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(275537, 18035, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - This is not a very compelling image.  The point of the photo is simple enough, but it doesn''t say much else to me.  It doesn''t really have a lot going for it.  There needs to be something more to this, like some kind of subject, but for the life of me I can''t think of what.  I guess I don''t have a lot to say about this.  I think an overhaul of the whole composition is about the only answer I have to solve the problems with this photo.  Give the viewers something to focus on and keep their attention.<br/> <br/>Technical - This is fairly well taken.  Snow shots are tough, especially when that''s pretty much what you were going for.  It seems a trite washed out nearest the grass.  Sacrificing some exposure time though may darken the greens in the grass a little more than you want though.  Tough call...<br/> <br/>Overall - This meets the challenge, but aside from that there isn''t too much I can tell you or suggest.  I think a nice clean spring slate would be the best place to start.  The snow is finally gone around here, for now.  Hope spring brings you lots of nice pics.  Good luck in future challenges. - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - This is not a very compelling image.  The point of the photo is simple enough, but it doesn''t say much else to me.  It doesn''t really have a lot going for it.  There needs to be something more to this, like some kind of subject, but for the life of me I can''t think of what.  I guess I don''t have a lot to say about this.  I think an overhaul of the whole composition is about the only answer I have to solve the problems with this photo.  Give the viewers something to focus on and keep their attention. Technical - This is fairly well taken.  Snow shots are tough, especially when that''s pretty much what you were going for.  It seems a trite washed out nearest the grass.  Sacrificing some exposure time though may darken the greens in the grass a little more than you want though.  Tough call... Overall - This meets the challenge, but aside from that there isn''t too much I can tell you or suggest.  I think a nice clean spring slate would be the best place to start.  The snow is finally gone around here, for now.  Hope spring brings you lots of nice pics.  Good luck in future challenges. - Inspzil', '2003-04-23 15:01:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(275544, 17640, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - I don''t have the first clue what you were shooting.  I''d like to say it meets the challenge, but I don''t know if it meets any challenge aside from abstract.  This is a tough one to critique.  My first suggestion would be to put clone some of the color from the top right corner and cover the whole image with that color and have some kind of fun abstract from it.  Personally, I don''t see anything in this image that is worth saving.<br/> <br/>Technical - N/A<br/> <br/>Overall - I''m not surprised one bit that this finished dead last.  I can''t find a single redeemable quality about it except that its a very small file and my dialup connection could load it very quickly.  Go back to the drawing board and start again.  I would like to know what this supposed to be a picture of though.  Good luck in future challenges.  I think from here, the only way to go is up!! - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - I don''t have the first clue what you were shooting.  I''d like to say it meets the challenge, but I don''t know if it meets any challenge aside from abstract.  This is a tough one to critique.  My first suggestion would be to put clone some of the color from the top right corner and cover the whole image with that color and have some kind of fun abstract from it.  Personally, I don''t see anything in this image that is worth saving. Technical - N/A Overall - I''m not surprised one bit that this finished dead last.  I can''t find a single redeemable quality about it except that its a very small file and my dialup connection could load it very quickly.  Go back to the drawing board and start again.  I would like to know what this supposed to be a picture of though.  Good luck in future challenges.  I think from here, the only way to go is up!! - Inspzil', '2003-04-23 15:06:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(275555, 18149, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi JDW...<br/> <br/>This photo is difficult for me to critique/comment because I''m one of the ones who did not think it was a strong tie to the ''weather'' challenge.  I do understand that horses are outdoor animals and they live out in the weather... this was the only tie i could come up with for this image.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I struggled with the photo.  The framing of this shot just left my eyes wandering.  I believe that for this shot to be interesting, you needed to either include the horse''s ears or his mouth, or both.  There doesn''t seem to be any continuity or natural flow from one point to the next in this photo...<br/> <br/>Keep up the good efforts :)<br/> <br/>BTW- I noticed that you are in Montana... have you ever had Moose Drool Stout from Big Sky Brewing Company? :)<br/> <br/>cheers...<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi JDW... This photo is difficult for me to critique/comment because I''m one of the ones who did not think it was a strong tie to the ''weather'' challenge.  I do understand that horses are outdoor animals and they live out in the weather... this was the only tie i could come up with for this image. Compositionally, I struggled with the photo.  The framing of this shot just left my eyes wandering.  I believe that for this shot to be interesting, you needed to either include the horse''s ears or his mouth, or both.  There doesn''t seem to be any continuity or natural flow from one point to the next in this photo... Keep up the good efforts :) BTW- I noticed that you are in Montana... have you ever had Moose Drool Stout from Big Sky Brewing Company? :) cheers... John Setzler', '2003-04-23 15:16:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(275641, 18113, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - This is my favorite kind of image to critique, not a bad image with loads of potential.  This image might have been better served to focus on the hill more as opposed to having it way off to the side.  I don''t know what the landscape had to offer over there though, so there may be a perfectly good reason why you didn''t.  The sky is awesome.  Great colors and very well exposed.  Too bad there weren''t a few more trees or anything to add a little texture to your silhouette.  Overall I say its a good composition.<br/> <br/>Technical - This is where this image falters a little and I think it''s all in the focus or lackthereof.  This shot really sharp with a little of anything as a silhouette would be awesome.  It needs to be sharp though with clearly visible silhouettes or it really loses our attention that the sky initially grabbed.  Very good job exposing this properly.  Your timing was excellent.<br/> <br/>Overall - My feeling about this image is that its pretty good, but really has a world of potential.  A couple of people in this pic with it a little closer to make them more distinguishable would be great.  Sometimes the people just aren''t around though, especially at sunrise.  This is a nice shot.  Good luck and keep shooting these sunrises. - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - This is my favorite kind of image to critique, not a bad image with loads of potential.  This image might have been better served to focus on the hill more as opposed to having it way off to the side.  I don''t know what the landscape had to offer over there though, so there may be a perfectly good reason why you didn''t.  The sky is awesome.  Great colors and very well exposed.  Too bad there weren''t a few more trees or anything to add a little texture to your silhouette.  Overall I say its a good composition. Technical - This is where this image falters a little and I think it''s all in the focus or lackthereof.  This shot really sharp with a little of anything as a silhouette would be awesome.  It needs to be sharp though with clearly visible silhouettes or it really loses our attention that the sky initially grabbed.  Very good job exposing this properly.  Your timing was excellent. Overall - My feeling about this image is that its pretty good, but really has a world of potential.  A couple of people in this pic with it a little closer to make them more distinguishable would be great.  Sometimes the people just aren''t around though, especially at sunrise.  This is a nice shot.  Good luck and keep shooting these sunrises. - Inspzil', '2003-04-23 16:22:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(275658, 17632, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC  hello bigboy....&lt;lol&gt; I feel like MaeWest.</b> <br/>P.S. Welcome to the group-great first entry.<br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-Yes <br/>Composition-Beautiful <br/>Background-Amazing <br/>My Opinion-Very nice shot. The colors in the sky are deep, rich, and vivid. The DOF is great....gotta love that Sony (pains me to say but true.) <br/>Looks like a tie on the lower 1/4 <i>to crop or not to crop</i>. Personally I don''t think the plane/tower add to the shot. The sky is so strong it can stand on it''s own. On the other hand......it allows the eye to cover the full shot and find suprise and interest. Nice shooting, good shot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-23 15:32:08.</i></td>', 'CC  hello bigboy....<lol> I feel like MaeWest. P.S. Welcome to the group-great first entry. Fits The Challenge-Yes Composition-Beautiful Background-Amazing My Opinion-Very nice shot. The colors in the sky are deep, rich, and vivid. The DOF is great....gotta love that Sony (pains me to say but true.) Looks like a tie on the lower 1/4 to crop or not to crop. Personally I don''t think the plane/tower add to the shot. The sky is so strong it can stand on it''s own. On the other hand......it allows the eye to cover the full shot and find suprise and interest. Nice shooting, good shot.', '2003-04-23 16:29:52.000000', '2003-04-23 16:32:08.000000', 0),
(275742, 18132, 1280, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comments by Grayce<br/>Well I guess if there is no significant weather happening nearby you go to the miniature world of snow globes. Imaginative!  I like studio shots so I give you credit for that. I suppose the idea could have worked but there is some glare on the globe.  <br/>I think for this to be more believable, the top of the globe should be cropped, as well as both sides and the bottom, so that only the scene showed.  <br/>The idea is clever, and definetly can be improved upon.  Put a little more energy and thought into the details and you will have an appealing image.<br/>Look forward to seeing more!<br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Grayce<br/>Regards, <br/> <br/>Grayce</td>', 'Critique Club Comments by GrayceWell I guess if there is no significant weather happening nearby you go to the miniature world of snow globes. Imaginative!  I like studio shots so I give you credit for that. I suppose the idea could have worked but there is some glare on the globe.  I think for this to be more believable, the top of the globe should be cropped, as well as both sides and the bottom, so that only the scene showed.  The idea is clever, and definetly can be improved upon.  Put a little more energy and thought into the details and you will have an appealing image.Look forward to seeing more!Regards, GrayceRegards,  Grayce', '2003-04-23 17:14:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(275765, 18248, 1280, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comments by Grayce<br/>Hi there!  The sky you captured here is a beautiful blue!  The clouds hanging in there add interest.<br/>A little detail is lost in the land.  If it was just a bit lighter, maybe the texture would be more visible.<br/>The coloring is nice, between the sky and the water and the little bit of green on the land.<br/>This would make a nice panoramic view too!<br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Grayce</td>', 'Critique Club Comments by GrayceHi there!  The sky you captured here is a beautiful blue!  The clouds hanging in there add interest.A little detail is lost in the land.  If it was just a bit lighter, maybe the texture would be more visible.The coloring is nice, between the sky and the water and the little bit of green on the land.This would make a nice panoramic view too!Regards, Grayce', '2003-04-23 17:27:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(275770, 18207, 4482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>THis is an above average shot which I think got the score it deserved.<br/> <br/>THEME: respected!<br/> <br/>COLOR AND FOCUS: great job on the colors! Your blue sky creates a nice contrast with the dark green areas. Your focus is good.<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION: IMO this seems like a "point and shoot" photo with not a lot of research done for composition... but then again, I''m often wrong!! The lines are ok but my eye isn''t drawn towards specific elements of the photo. Nothing really stands out. There''s nothing wrong with that  but I think that''s where you coulda gotten a few extra points. YA know that whole "WOW" factor that DPC members look for. :o)<br/> <br/>All in all a good shot! Keep it up!!<br/> <br/>Yanik</td>', 'Greetings from the CC! THis is an above average shot which I think got the score it deserved. THEME: respected! COLOR AND FOCUS: great job on the colors! Your blue sky creates a nice contrast with the dark green areas. Your focus is good. COMPOSITION: IMO this seems like a "point and shoot" photo with not a lot of research done for composition... but then again, I''m often wrong!! The lines are ok but my eye isn''t drawn towards specific elements of the photo. Nothing really stands out. There''s nothing wrong with that  but I think that''s where you coulda gotten a few extra points. YA know that whole "WOW" factor that DPC members look for. :o) All in all a good shot! Keep it up!! Yanik', '2003-04-23 17:34:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(275775, 17921, 1280, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comments by Grayce<br/>Wow!  Your first entry and a ribbon!!! Congratulations.  I liked this from the first time I saw it and scored high on it. Certainly worthy of the ribbon!<br/>The tones in this make it special.  The exposure is very nice, allowing variations to be visbible.  <br/>The rays glowing down really steal the show.  It''s just so moody, and inspiring at the same time.  The way the rays hit the water is really special.  Not a scene one sees every day.<br/>The border is well chosen, not being in competition with the subject, but rather complementing it.<br/>Overall very nice!<br/>Welcome to DPC!!!<br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Grayce</td>', 'Critique Club Comments by GrayceWow!  Your first entry and a ribbon!!! Congratulations.  I liked this from the first time I saw it and scored high on it. Certainly worthy of the ribbon!The tones in this make it special.  The exposure is very nice, allowing variations to be visbible.  The rays glowing down really steal the show.  It''s just so moody, and inspiring at the same time.  The way the rays hit the water is really special.  Not a scene one sees every day.The border is well chosen, not being in competition with the subject, but rather complementing it.Overall very nice!Welcome to DPC!!!Regards, Grayce', '2003-04-23 17:37:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(275811, 18167, 4482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>You had some stiff competition ad you stil managed a top 40 finish! Good work!<br/> <br/>I like this shot very much.... it relaxes me...<br/> <br/>THEME: respected hands up!<br/> <br/>COLOR AND FOCUS: both are spot on. From the light beige to the darker browns mixed in with some white, grey and a touch of blue. Magnifique!<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION: I see research in this shot, especially with the angle chosen. IMO your crop is good. Cutting out more reeds would''ve lost the magestic quality of them.<br/> <br/>All in all a great shot! Even the border fits! Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Yanik</td>', 'Greetings from the CC! You had some stiff competition ad you stil managed a top 40 finish! Good work! I like this shot very much.... it relaxes me... THEME: respected hands up! COLOR AND FOCUS: both are spot on. From the light beige to the darker browns mixed in with some white, grey and a touch of blue. Magnifique! COMPOSITION: I see research in this shot, especially with the angle chosen. IMO your crop is good. Cutting out more reeds would''ve lost the magestic quality of them. All in all a great shot! Even the border fits! Keep up the good work! Yanik', '2003-04-23 17:50:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(275814, 18257, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Tarbini...<br/> <br/>This is a very strong cloudscape.  The cloud patterns and the color variations make it work very nicely.  I''m a bad choice of people to critique photos like this because I personally don''t care for cloudscapes.  My personal taste includes some amount of ''land'' in the image to add perspective to the cloudscape.  This is not saying that this is not a great shot because it is :)<br/> <br/>I think your final score here definitely supports the overall opinion of the site... 6.4 is a great finish...<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Tarbini... This is a very strong cloudscape.  The cloud patterns and the color variations make it work very nicely.  I''m a bad choice of people to critique photos like this because I personally don''t care for cloudscapes.  My personal taste includes some amount of ''land'' in the image to add perspective to the cloudscape.  This is not saying that this is not a great shot because it is :) I think your final score here definitely supports the overall opinion of the site... 6.4 is a great finish... Keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2003-04-23 17:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
